# Kello01a route by player input (item98e): the authored valley loop to the start of the north
# bank climb, where the walker meets the authored invisible BSP wall and stops, alive.
#
# Start: MapInfo `Kello0` (XIDMaps.Kello01) `NextMapLevelWithUnr = "Kello01b.unr"`, one
# objective `[0 P] Find the chalet`, player at PlayerStart0 (-3005.8, 6127.0, 90.6) UU,
# yaw -26864 (Unreal units), health 150, loadout from the map-entry AcceptInventory path
# (magnum group 3, FusilPompe group 9, FusilChasse group 10, with ammo).
#
# The waypoint chain is the walkable route the map's own simulation produces: a breadth-first
# search over the `PlayerSim` (the same fixed-step walker `--play` drives: MINFLOORZ 0.7,
# MAXSTEPHEIGHT 35 UU, gravity, water volumes) from PlayerStart0 along the valley loop the
# BSP zone-connectivity chain (11->8->7->9->10->12->13->3->2->5->6) and the navigation graph
# both follow: descend the bowl south-east, round the valley south to y~-4900 and west to the
# lake. item98c continued across lake Keelownee with jump strokes; item98d measured that the
# lake's `WaterVolume0`/`WaterVolume1` are `bPainCausing=true, DamagePerSec=60,
# DamageType=DTDrowned`, so the crossing is lethal on touch and the ice floes do not span it.
# item98e re-mapped the floes/ice and the dry north band: the floes do not form a jumpable
# chain (gaps up to 1200 UU against a ~417 UU retail running jump), so the route leaves the
# valley north toward the dry band. The walker reaches ~(-4200,-776) on the band's south face
# and is stopped there by the authored invisible solid BSP sheet (Model207, the triangle
# (-3664,-1440,-1344)-(-5280,896,3776)-(-5280,896,-1344)) that spans x[-5280,-3664]
# y[-1440,896] z[-1344,3776]. Coordinates are Unreal units; times are seconds. Input only:
# `goto`, `select_weapon`/`track`/`fire`/`reload` for the authored soldier fights. No
# teleport, weapon grant, item, set_goal or control override.
